                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers[/h1]\n\nYou can view my review & gameplay here: https://youtu.be/-WB5B5WVGLw\n\nI'm giving a neutral recommendation. Please know what you're getting before you buy. This game is solely shooting a basketball through a hoop in 3 different VR environments with in-game music.  You can also customize the color of your basketball.\n\nThe hoop looks too big.  It looks exactly the same in all 3 VR enviroments and has no net.  The game does keep track of how many baskets you made, but it doesn't keep track of whether it's a 2 or 3 pointer and it doesn't seem to care whether you made the basket on your side or the opposite side.\n\nThe throwing motion is not realistic (of course how can it be without any weight to the basketball?).  But you do have to move your hand faster the farther away you are from the basket.  It's very challenging to make a 3 point shot.  If you're straight on, the backboard behaves realistically, but if you're at an angle, it does not.  The rim also seems to very hard as it bounces many balls right off so there's no \"shooter's touch\" in this simulation.  You cannot dribble (well you can shoot down and grab then shoot down and rapidly grab again but that isn't really dribbling).  You move by teleporting only. There is no snap turning or smooth turning.\n\nThe graphics are subpar. However, the music soundtrack is pretty neat (IMO).  The dev promised future updates, but it looks like an abandoned project. Please note: I bought this game on steam for $1.24 USD, but the video is for the Oculus Store version which went free to play.\n\nRating 5/10. Neutral recommendation.",
